ll","It may repeat","It must be text","It must reference another table"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"A primary key uniquely identifies a row and cannot be null.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"It is unique and non-null","option_b":"It may repeat","option_c":"It must be text","option_d":"It must reference another table"},{"id":"db-1-4","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Foreign Keys","question_text":"What does a foreign key primarily enforce?","options":["Referential integrity","Sort order","Column encryption","Query caching"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"It constrains values to referenced candidate-key values.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"Referential integrity","option_b":"Sort order","option_c":"Column encryption","option_d":"Query caching"},{"id":"db-1-5","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Normalization","question_text":"Which normal form removes partial dependency on a composite key?","options":["Second normal form","First normal form","Third normal form","BCNF only"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"2NF removes partial dependencies on a candidate key.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.2,"option_a":"Second normal form","option_b":"First normal form","option_c":"Third normal form","option_d":"BCNF only"},{"id":"db-1-6","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Transactions","question_text":"Which ACID property ensures committed data survives failure?","options":["Durability","Atomicity","Isolation","Consistency"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Durability preserves committed changes.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.3,"option_a":"Durability","option_b":"Atomicity","option_c":"Isolation","option_d":"Consistency"},{"id":"db-1-7","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Transactions","question_text":"Which ACID property makes a transaction all-or-nothing?","options":["Atomicity","Isolation","Durability","Availability"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Atomicity prevents partial transactions.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.4,"option_a":"Atomicity","option_b":"Isolation","option_c":"Durability","option_d":"Availability"},{"id":"db-1-8","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Indexes","question_text":"What is the usual trade-off of adding an index?","options":["Faster reads but extra storage and write cost","Faster writes with no cost","Automatic normalization","Guaranteed uniqueness for every index"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Indexes accelerate matching reads but must be maintained on writes.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.5,"option_a":"Faster reads but extra storage and write cost","option_b":"Faster writes with no cost","option_c":"Automatic normalization","option_d":"Guaranteed uniqueness for every index"},{"id":"db-1-9","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"JOIN","question_text":"Which join retains every row from the left table?","options":["LEFT JOIN","INNER JOIN","CROSS JOIN","SELF JOIN"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"LEFT JOIN preserves all left rows.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"LEFT JOIN","option_b":"INNER JOIN","option_c":"CROSS JOIN","option_d":"SELF JOIN"},{"id":"db-1-10","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"NULL","question_text":"Which predicate correctly tests missing SQL values?","options":["IS NULL","= NULL","== NULL","NULL()"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"NULL uses IS NULL because equality with NULL is unknown.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"IS NULL","option_b":"= NULL","option_c":"== NULL","option_d":"NULL()"},{"id":"db-1-11","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Grouping","question_text":"A query selects department and COUNT(*). What else is normally required?","options":["GROUP BY department","ORDER BY department","HAVING department","DISTINCT COUNT"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Non-aggregated selected columns normally belong in GROUP 