). What else is normally required?","options":["GROUP BY department","ORDER BY department","HAVING department","DISTINCT COUNT"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Non-aggregated selected columns normally belong in GROUP BY.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.4,"option_a":"GROUP BY department","option_b":"ORDER BY department","option_c":"HAVING department","option_d":"DISTINCT COUNT"},{"id":"db-2-12","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Isolation","question_text":"In a recruitment database scenario: What anomaly is prevented when a transaction cannot read uncommitted changes?","options":["Dirty read","Lost index","Dead column","Schema drift"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Dirty reads observe another transaction's uncommitted work.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.5,"option_a":"Dirty read","option_b":"Lost index","option_c":"Dead column","option_d":"Schema drift"},{"id":"db-2-13","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Query Logic","question_text":"In a recruitment database scenario: COUNT(column_name) differs from COUNT(*) because it does what?","options":["Ignores NULL values in that column","Counts distinct values only","Counts tables","Returns text"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"COUNT(column) ignores NULL; COUNT(*) counts rows.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"Ignores NULL values in that column","option_b":"Counts distinct values only","option_c":"Counts tables","option_d":"Returns text"},{"id":"db-2-14","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Set Operations","question_text":"In a recruitment database scenario: What does UNION do by default?","options":["Removes duplicate rows","Keeps all duplicates","Joins columns by keys","Updates both queries"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"UNION applies duplicate elimination; UNION ALL does not.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"Removes duplicate rows","option_b":"Keeps all duplicates","option_c":"Joins columns by ke